Subject: d3d11: route On12 state objects, samplers and scissor rectangles

Blend, depth-stencil, rasterizer and sampler state objects had no backend:
every Create*State on a standalone On12 device returned
DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED, and OMSetBlendState, OMSetDepthStencilState,
RSSetState, {VS,PS}SetSamplers and RSSetScissorRects returned after a WARN.
Core exports 35-41 have existed since the PSO component work but nothing in
the frontend used them, and without samplers no texture can be filtered.

Each of the four state structures now embeds a backend child and the core's
pipeline-state handle. When the device's backend provides create_state,
d3d_*_state_create makes the core object instead of a WineD3D one, after the
state is in the device's description tree. Wine already deduplicates
identical descriptions through those trees, so each unique state reaches the
driver once. The public refcount holds one backend reference, as buffers'
does, and each binding holds another; the last one destroys the core object
and removes the tree entry.

That last step has a race the WineD3D path did not need to consider: an
identical Create*State can find the entry and re-reference it between the
final decref and the removal. Releases take the wined3d mutex around their
decref, and the destroy callback rechecks the backend refcount under the
mutex and keeps the state if it was resurrected.

D3D11.1-only features are refused with DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED rather than
silently dropped: blend logic ops, ForcedSampleCount and conservative
rasterization. Binding goes through exports 39-41 and the new
SetSamplersV1 and SetScissorRectsV1 (ordinals 53, 54); sampler creation
through CreateSamplerStateV1 (52). Getters report the retained bindings,
blend factor, sample mask, stencil reference and scissor rectangles.
ClearState resets all of them.

The new backend ops are designated members, absent from the WineD3D table,
so ordinary devices keep their WineD3D state objects. The ten exports
resolve as one required group.

Requires WineD3D11On12{CreateBlendState,CreateDepthStencilState,
CreateRasterizerState,DestroyPipelineState,SetBlendState,
SetDepthStencilState,SetRasterizerState}V1 (ordinals 35-41) and
WineD3D11On12{CreateSamplerState,SetSamplers,SetScissorRects}V1 (52-54).
Applies after patches 0002-0029 to WineCX
7dbc5b5322a6ef3fb04bdc643c64b188fd641149.

